    "long_instructions": "## Store Backup Data\r\n\r\n**Goal:** Create a local `localCountries` array and a function to display it. This proves your \"Safety Net\" works before we add the complex internet logic.\r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Create a `const` array named `localCountries` with **three objects** inside (each having `name` and `population`).\r\n\r\n2. Create an arrow function named `renderBackup`. Inside, write a loop that adds each country from your array to the `outputElement.innerHTML`.\r\n\r\n3. Call `renderBackup()` at the bottom of your code. You should see your local data appear on the screen!\r\n\r\n",
